  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.0.0 — Architecture overhaul: beats sockets by 15%\n• IoUringPipeScheduler: custom PipeScheduler runs all pipe continuations on\n  the IO loop thread. Eliminates ThreadPool hops for both recv and send paths.\n• Inline HTTP processing: Kestrel HTTP pipeline runs on the IO thread\n  (like UnsafePreferInlineScheduling). Zero cross-thread signaling.\n• Non-blocking send: IValueTaskSource-based send completion. Send loop yields\n  after SQE submit, resumes inline on CQE. Zero-alloc send path.\n• Connection slot array: replaces ConcurrentDictionary with O(1) direct index.\n• Pre-pinned recv buffer: eliminates per-recv Pin()/Dispose().\n• Fix SetSqeFd infinite recursion bug (stack overflow when fd registration fails).\n• Coalesced PipeScheduler wakeups: flag-based eventfd dedup.\n\nBenchmark: json scenario, 56-core Intel Xeon Gold 6330, kernel 6.8.0\n  256c: 2,043K RPS (+9% vs sockets)\n  512c: 2,499K RPS (+13% vs sockets)\n  1024c: 2,829K RPS (+15% vs sockets)\n  CPU usage: 50% (sockets: 90%) — 1.9x more efficient per CPU cycle\n  Lock contention: 50/s (sockets: 1,994/s)\n  GC time: 0% | Allocation rate: 3.8M B/s (below sockets)\n\nv1.2.0 — Re-enable buffer ring + SQPOLL mode\n• Re-enable provided buffer ring (multishot recv) — stalling bug fixed\n  on kernel 6.6+. Eliminates per-recv Pin()/Dispose() overhead.\n  Controlled via EnableBufferRing option (default: true).\n• Add SQPOLL mode support (EnableSqPoll option). Kernel polls the SQ ring,\n  eliminating io_uring_enter syscalls. Requires CAP_SYS_NICE or root.\n• Ring constructor now accepts setup flags for SQPOLL and future kernel features.\n• BufferRingSize option for tuning buffer ring depth (default: 256).\n\nv1.1.0 — Performance: lock-free send path\n• Send operations are now enqueued to the IO loop via ConcurrentQueue + eventfd\n  instead of acquiring SubmitLock per send. Eliminates 90K+/s lock contentions\n  on multi-core machines.\n• IO loop is now the sole SQ producer — all submissions are batched into a\n  single io_uring_enter per loop iteration.\n• Reduces per-send syscalls from 1 each to 0 (batched with recv/accept work).\n\nv1.0.1 — Bug fix\n• Fix IOSQE_BUFFER_SELECT constant: was 1<<3 (0x08), now 1<<5 (0x20)\n  Matches kernel definition. Fixes EFAULT when using buffer rings with recv.\n• Add test project with 10 tests (unit + integration)\n• Add InternalsVisibleTo for test project\n\nv1.0.0 — Initial release\n• Drop-in io_uring transport via UseIoUring()\n• Multishot recv with buffer rings\n• Zero-copy send (SEND_ZC)\n• Registered file descriptors\n• Targets net8.0, net9.0, net10.0",
